# Railway

> Railway is an infrastructure platform that simplifies your stack from servers to observability with a single, scalable, easy-to-use platform. Railway's superior developer experience makes it easy to deploy cloud infrastructure, full-stack applications, and websites.

## About Railway

- [Railway Features](https://railway.com/features.md): An unparalleled developer experience for infrastructure — build, deploy, network, scale, observe, and secure your apps
- [Railway Customers](https://railway.com/customers.md): Loved by developers at 31% of the F500. Hear how Railway powers businesses across AI, Fintech, B2B SaaS, and more
- [About Railway](https://railway.com/about.md): Railway is building the cloud computing stack that unburdens developers, so they can focus on what matters
- [Railway Careers](https://railway.com/careers.md): Railway is hiring engineers and designers to rebuild the cloud computing stack

## For AI Agents

- [Railway for AI Agents](https://railway.com/agents.md): Critical setup instructions for agents — CLI setup with `bash <(curl -fsSL cli.new) --agents -y`, local MCP and agent skills, optional remote MCP, and core use cases (deploy, databases, volumes, functions, config).
- [railway.com/index.md](https://railway.com/index.md): The same agent setup briefing, served at the site root
- [Railway Remote MCP Server](https://railway.com/mcp.md): Connect AI coding agents to Railway over OAuth — no local install, no CLI login, no token files
- [Authenticating to Railway](https://railway.com/auth.md): The four ways to hold a Railway credential — CLI login, remote MCP over OAuth, public API tokens, and Login with Railway — with the exact headers to send

## Machine-Readable Endpoints

- [AI catalog (ARD)](https://railway.com/.well-known/ai-catalog.json): Agentic Resource Discovery catalog of every agentic resource — MCP server, API, and instruction pages — with stable identifiers
- [API catalog](https://railway.com/.well-known/api-catalog): RFC 9727 linkset naming every Railway API, its docs, its auth metadata, and its status page
- [MCP server card](https://railway.com/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json): Identity and transport for the remote MCP server at `mcp.railway.com`
- Public API (GraphQL): `https://backboard.railway.com/graphql/v2` — single endpoint, schema by introspection
- [Template deploy manifests](https://railway.com/deploy/llms.txt): Machine-readable deploy manifest per template — one line each with validation status; inputs and deploy commands inline at https://railway.com/deploy/llms-full.txt, JSON index at https://railway.com/deploy/index.json, per-template manifests at https://railway.com/deploy/{template}/manifest.json
- [OpenAPI description](https://railway.com/openapi.json): OpenAPI 3.1 for the GraphQL entrypoint and the OAuth 2.0 / OIDC endpoints
- [API reliability](https://railway.com/api-reliability.md): Errors and error codes, rate limits and headers, retry guidance, and the versioning/deprecation policy
- OpenID Connect discovery: `https://backboard.railway.com/oauth/.well-known/openid-configuration`

## Product Details

- [Railway Sandboxes](https://railway.com/sandboxes.md): Linux VMs with coding agents preinstalled, private networking, checkpoints, forks, and usage-based pricing
- [Free VMs, no sign up](https://railway.com/free-vm.md): `ssh railway.new` gets a free Linux VM with coding agents preinstalled and a preview URL, no account needed; agents can use it too
- [Railway Pricing](https://railway.com/pricing.md): Plans, per-second usage rates for CPU/memory/disk/egress/storage, and committed spend
- [Railway Enterprise](https://railway.com/enterprise.md): World-class scale, security, and support for organizations and enterprise teams
- [Railway Domains](https://railway.com/domains.md): Register and manage custom domains for your Railway services, with automatic SSL certificates
- [Railway Mobile App](https://railway.com/mobile.md): Deploy, monitor, and manage your services from anywhere
- [Migrate from Heroku](https://railway.com/heroku.md): Railway is the Heroku alternative with cheaper pricing, faster builds, and better developer experience
- [Railway Template Marketplace](https://railway.com/deploy.md): Template categories and the most deployed one-click templates
- [Railway AI Templates](https://railway.com/deploy/category/ai.md): One-click AI templates like Ollama, Open WebUI, and vector databases, with FAQs on hosting AI apps
- [Railway Templates](https://railway.com/llms-templates.md): One-click deploy templates with architecture details, service configs, and READMEs
- [Railway Product Changelog](https://railway.com/llms-changelog.md): Product changelog entries with titles, dates, and links
- [Railway Changelog Index](https://railway.com/changelog.md): Product updates ordered by date; individual entries are available at /changelog/<slug>.md

## Programs & Events

- [Railway Affiliate Program](https://railway.com/affiliate-program.md): Earn 15% commission on every invoice from your Railway referrals for 12 months after signup
- [Railway Template Kickback Program](https://railway.com/open-source-kickback.md): Earn 25% revenue commission whenever someone deploys your template on Railway
- [Railway Open Source Partner Program](https://railway.com/partners.md): Turn your open source project into a deployable Railway template, support users directly, and earn commission on every deployment
- [Railway Bug Bounty](https://railway.com/bug-bounty.md): Railway pays researchers for valid security vulnerability reports, scored against CVSS 3.1
- [Railway Launch Week 01](https://railway.com/launch-week-01.md): Five feature-packed days from September 25–29, 2023 bringing new ways to scale Railway applications globally

